# Feature Removal Documentation Sweep

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

When **removing** a plot module, API field, SPA tab, or analysis surface that users or operators could discover in docs, sweep related prose in the same task.

## Trigger conditions

- Deleting plot builders under `hpcperfstats/analysis/metrics/lib/plot/` or removing API/SPA consumers.
- Removing Job Detail tabs, Extended Search fields, or metric catalog entries.
- Retiring architecture-specific surfaces (for example heatmap, KNL peaks) while leaving related metrics.

## Required sweep (grep-driven)

| Area | Action |
|------|--------|
| `docs/using-the-website-as-a-researcher.md` | Remove or rewrite sections that reference the retired surface; add history row when user-visible. |
| `hpcperfstats/analysis/README_ARCH_AGNOSTIC.md` | Remove stale capability bullets. |
| `docs/`, `artifacts/` gap/compliance reports | Remove or update matrices that still list the feature. |
| Frontend `variableMetadata*.js` | Remove tooltips/labels for retired fields when UI no longer shows them. |

## Overlap

- **`researcher-job-detail-doc-sync.mdc`** — additive job-detail changes.
- **`end-to-end-feature-wiring-contract.mdc`** — wiring removal across layers.
